## Use it

```toml
[dependencies]
{%- if publish_crate %}
{{ crate_name }} = "<version>"
{%- else %}
{{ crate_name }} = { git = "https://github.com/{{ github_owner }}/{{ project_name }}", tag = "<tag>" }
{%- endif %}
```
{%- if publish_crate %}

`cargo add {{ crate_name }}` writes the latest version.
{%- else %}

Replace `<tag>` with a release tag, such as the
[latest](https://github.com/{{ github_owner }}/{{ project_name }}/releases/latest).
{%- if visibility == 'private' %}
The repository is private, so have Cargo fetch it with your Git credentials. Add this to your
`~/.cargo/config.toml`:

```toml
[net]
git-fetch-with-cli = true
```
{%- endif %}
